#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059402 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23637774-8d69-500d-8cb0-5e41a0207542" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Rational Expressions Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "3b9c93fe-82ac-58c5-b14a-9bcd30b1f0e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-3175" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\dfrac{\\cos{x}}{1-\\cos^2{x}}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the denominator using\n\n$$\n1-\\cos^2 x = \\sin^2 x\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\cos{x}}{1-\\cos^2{x}} = \\dfrac{\\cos{x}}{\\sin^2{x}}\n$$\n\nNext, we simplify the expression by separating out the factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin^{2} x} &= \\frac{\\cos x \\cdot 1}{\\sin x \\cdot \\sin x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sin x} \\\\\n&= \\cot x\\csc x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\cos{x}}{1-\\cos^2{x}}=\\cot{x}\\csc{x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059403 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b05f4be1-95d4-5137-bbaa-71c95862bb59" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions by Factoring an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "e5821060-9f69-5df5-9456-a4574e92e910" :question/math-academy-id "e-3176" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\cos^2 x}{1-\\sin x}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the numerator using\n\n$$\n1-\\sin^2 x = \\cos^2 x\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\cos^2 x}{1-\\sin x} = \\dfrac{1-\\sin^2 x}{1-\\sin x}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor the numerator as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1 - \\sin^{2} x}{1 - \\sin x} &= ((1 - \\sin x)(1 + \\sin x))/(1 - \\sin x) \\\\\n&= ((1 - \\sin x)(1 + \\sin x))/(1 - \\sin x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 + \\sin x}{1} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\sin x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\cos^2 x}{1-\\sin x} = 1 + \\sin x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059410 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e85a2d68-d49f-5bf4-ab62-13ad8c35b0d4" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expression Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "056204bc-53b9-5a32-a53c-0f728729fd9f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3332" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $3\\cos^2 x \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses and simplify the resulting expression:\n\n$$\n3\\cos^2 x \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right) = 3\\cos^2 x \\sec^2 x - 3\\cos^2 x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the identity\n\n$$\n\\sec x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}\n$$\n\nto further simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3\\cos^{2} x\\sec^{2} x - 3\\cos^{2} x &= 3\\cos^{2} x \\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\cos x})^{2} - 3\\cos^{2} x \\\\\n&= 3\\cos^{2} x \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cos^{2} x} - 3\\cos^{2} x \\\\\n&= \\frac{3\\cos^{2} x}{\\cos^{2} x} - 3\\cos^{2} x \\\\\n&= \\frac{3\\cos^{2} x}{\\cos^{2} x} - 3\\cos^{2} x \\\\\n&= 3 - 3\\cos^{2} x \\\\\n&= 3(1 - \\cos^{2} x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the identity\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x = 1-\\cos^2 x\n$$\n\nto rewrite the expression in the parentheses, as follows:\n\n$$\n3(1-\\cos^2 x) = 3\\cdot \\sin^2 x = 3\\sin^2 x\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3\\cos^2 x \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right)= 3\\sin^2 x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b05f4be1-95d4-5137-bbaa-71c95862bb59" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions by Factoring an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caffff83-e7da-5a66-a046-2750216af54a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256038} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f976e9-845d-585c-a30a-d5db1ba6d2bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256039} {:answer/id #uuid "3e51a5b7-8e4f-5e1e-be08-a80125fdebc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256040} {:answer/id #uuid "8a6b5628-8739-524c-8d86-9066732bff0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256041} {:answer/id #uuid "5fdfdfd9-9b44-58f7-9ad6-64002e5c9515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a6b5628-8739-524c-8d86-9066732bff0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256041} :answer-field/id #uuid "4642b8ad-4d35-59d8-843c-930abe290c27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256037}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a411090-86b1-5b85-b794-25064aecdcb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-119864" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1}=\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the numerator as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1} & =\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =-(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1}=-(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b05f4be1-95d4-5137-bbaa-71c95862bb59" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions by Factoring an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ca0dd09-6e25-5bee-a23b-0c57f4f75249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256045} {:answer/id #uuid "23189c1b-74a4-50e4-9028-6d663e2f2d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256046} {:answer/id #uuid "694cb260-f7a1-547d-a315-72ae5e0e2759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256047} {:answer/id #uuid "a82ff050-5a53-53c0-9141-19021f3d4e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256048} {:answer/id #uuid "6c62c9b8-f4ea-5067-9ac3-86e57d6069aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23189c1b-74a4-50e4-9028-6d663e2f2d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256046} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd4170a1-69b2-5bb9-92f3-2a3f0d4e7e97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256044}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59727a48-6801-5fec-a4c7-d19432c127ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-119866" :question/problem "$\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the denominator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)^{2}}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the denominator as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)^{2}}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)}{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\cancel{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)}}{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cancel{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b05f4be1-95d4-5137-bbaa-71c95862bb59" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions by Factoring an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7365985e-3e60-5a48-b065-21787d91e6ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256052} {:answer/id #uuid "efc65452-687d-5bdb-81d9-12e5d3cea55b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256053} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8179a5-6692-5698-b59a-14371af4b5f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256054} {:answer/id #uuid "958597d5-311a-5dc8-acda-9e0b6bb92355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256055} {:answer/id #uuid "ce0a71c8-6512-54bf-927d-d56e9f7448fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "958597d5-311a-5dc8-acda-9e0b6bb92355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256055} :answer-field/id #uuid "c52cabae-0f6c-5b15-86a0-50ee6f183fa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256051}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cd988279-04e9-5dc2-8817-ea35dc50b687" :question/math-academy-id "q-119869" :question/problem "If $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{2{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{1}{f(x)},$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the denominator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{2{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{2(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the denominator as difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{2(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{2\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-2(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23637774-8d69-500d-8cb0-5e41a0207542" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Rational Expressions Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3de64ba8-4a91-5aa2-a18a-fd4efc1f0b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256059} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5e7e9b-bc8f-5775-9485-47af8375b211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256060} {:answer/id #uuid "ddcb8b3b-f528-54f0-bc07-fdef2ba0da80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256061} {:answer/id #uuid "27bb5c10-5f4f-521f-b09d-12b0cc4ce9fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256062} {:answer/id #uuid "89351033-f1b7-5db0-91f1-b329f9030bfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddcb8b3b-f528-54f0-bc07-fdef2ba0da80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256061} :answer-field/id #uuid "d83573d3-58b0-50f3-a5d4-26d2ca1d1119" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256058}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1b9f7423-53ea-52bd-a634-039b96bcb018" :question/math-academy-id "q-1583" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡A}-\\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡A}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the definition of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡A$ to rewrite the second term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡A}-\\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡A} & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡A}-{tan}^{2}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡A}-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡A}{{cos}^{2}⁡A} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡A}{{cos}^{2}⁡A}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the identity $1-{sin}^{2}⁡A={cos}^{2}⁡A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡A}{{cos}^{2}⁡A} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡A}{{cos}^{2}⁡A}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡A}-\\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡A}=1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23637774-8d69-500d-8cb0-5e41a0207542" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Rational Expressions Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c46f0f01-bd4f-518d-831d-19504cbf049a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256066} {:answer/id #uuid "5fdb5ea8-a48e-5560-881c-71cb67cdf3d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256067} {:answer/id #uuid "b7174108-255f-5102-bf20-d44a1f3c9894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256068} {:answer/id #uuid "0bc3e2cd-d241-5431-abcc-228e3997edc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256069} {:answer/id #uuid "a3fd94af-3e25-5afd-9a3f-2261b108cd6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3fd94af-3e25-5afd-9a3f-2261b108cd6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256070} :answer-field/id #uuid "b12e7b03-e883-5d78-9a0f-d985a3b8a522" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256065}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c9911307-0112-59e4-9738-ff3a7034ff3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-1584" :question/problem "$\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t-1}{{cos}^{2}⁡t{tan}^{2}⁡t}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡t={sin}^{2}⁡t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t-1}{{cos}^{2}⁡t{tan}^{2}⁡t} & =\\frac{-1\\cdot (1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}{{cos}^{2}⁡t{tan}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}⁡t}{{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the denominator using the definition of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta $ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{sin}^{2}⁡t}{{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡t} & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}⁡t}{{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot {(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}⁡t}{{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot (\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{{cos}^{2}⁡t})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}⁡t}{(\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡t}{{cos}^{2}⁡t})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}⁡t}{(\\frac{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡t}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}⁡t}{{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡t}}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡t}} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t-1}{{cos}^{2}⁡t{tan}^{2}⁡t}=-1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23637774-8d69-500d-8cb0-5e41a0207542" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Rational Expressions Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8523c015-4a03-5945-9b2b-ea28913ce7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256073} {:answer/id #uuid "8a93beb2-cc46-5ede-930f-d011353b6f55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256074} {:answer/id #uuid "9782a73d-6468-5dae-b324-07d8baac92d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256075} {:answer/id #uuid "23b11503-db90-5c2c-932e-630ce828ac49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256076} {:answer/id #uuid "97a359f3-9857-5386-839f-00bf419d76d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9782a73d-6468-5dae-b324-07d8baac92d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256075} :answer-field/id #uuid "712f941d-2256-5287-82a0-7372e40f7c34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256072}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d58ed21c-2695-53ea-85df-0c7a82fbe9a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-23526" :question/problem "$\\frac{1-2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "Since both fractions are over a common denominator, we can add them. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1-2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta $ to simplify the expression in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23637774-8d69-500d-8cb0-5e41a0207542" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Rational Expressions Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a64978c-5658-51d7-8e26-54f304d0b377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256080} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b253af-291a-55f0-983c-1cff1fd09e4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256081} {:answer/id #uuid "572b3dc9-c4fe-546b-a5c0-c7b6ce855642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256082} {:answer/id #uuid "34321c77-8813-5672-ad01-3ad1d91d4f01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256083} {:answer/id #uuid "2e1ce960-9e6c-5d4e-88c2-4237a9359f6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34321c77-8813-5672-ad01-3ad1d91d4f01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256083} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a0e142c-6ab2-5b2c-8fe6-38b00083b9e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256079}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e2ba7e3-c56a-5de4-af53-4b9170dfe278" :question/math-academy-id "q-24322" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{3\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the expression using the definitions of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta $ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta $:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{3\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{3(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{3(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{3(\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{3{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use $1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta $ to simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{3{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{3{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}{3\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{3\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{1}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e85a2d68-d49f-5bf4-ab62-13ad8c35b0d4" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expression Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa2b4ae3-122c-51e7-9a7d-264bdf46b175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256087} {:answer/id #uuid "3bee3c4e-865e-5489-aa24-85733da68299" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256088} {:answer/id #uuid "ce56bfb9-f3f6-501c-aa33-8d7aa8353783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256089} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c7796b-60d1-5445-8c80-e7494e342810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256090} {:answer/id #uuid "c40149fa-c02a-505f-b83d-80b3be9bd219" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c40149fa-c02a-505f-b83d-80b3be9bd219" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256091} :answer-field/id #uuid "427db10e-029f-5de1-825e-9d84e67c5be4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256086}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ddc6f5d8-fb4c-500a-bd59-94e92ff60083" :question/math-academy-id "q-43308" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )(1+\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta )?$" :question/worked-solution "First, use the identity $\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )(1+\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta ) & =(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )(1+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & =(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we expand the parentheses in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b05f4be1-95d4-5137-bbaa-71c95862bb59" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions by Factoring an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "901fb9c5-25ff-5cfd-ad3a-5e4dd673bbb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 - \\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058610} {:answer/id #uuid "938f75f5-7827-5d56-8bcf-6ba9760488c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos x - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058611} {:answer/id #uuid "edd3e6f8-5a29-545d-ab4d-ed9f68fab862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos x - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058612} {:answer/id #uuid "501d4a84-03d5-5012-8a5c-cdfa69819cf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058613} {:answer/id #uuid "79d9be8d-49f3-571c-9564-1890c8c04089" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79d9be8d-49f3-571c-9564-1890c8c04089" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058614} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fbdca89-59b7-52fd-85f3-bf7334d417d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058609}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6649e183-eb4d-5947-a240-b0aee73aa4fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-65182" :question/problem "If $\\frac{1 - \\cos x}{\\sin^{2} x} = (1)/(f(x))$, then $f(x) =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the denominator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the denominator as difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256092 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e85a2d68-d49f-5bf4-ab62-13ad8c35b0d4" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expression Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82a8fcc8-196c-5cf1-9a16-882f30365fee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256094} {:answer/id #uuid "26799556-3330-5e27-a5a3-1331b7d712c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{csc}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256095} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbdae94-6e08-5e31-bbb0-d9a492749fbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256096} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a657db-49bc-5af5-a980-ed596b717204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256097} {:answer/id #uuid "ecbbb73b-bcac-55d0-804e-cb4bc71b4712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bbdae94-6e08-5e31-bbb0-d9a492749fbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256096} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fd41a37-2bf5-55bf-95ad-8d68d60e4407" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256093}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3ef0d2b-1955-501d-b9e1-d5aa56bd2220" :question/math-academy-id "q-65211" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ to further simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the identity ${sin}^{2}⁡x=1-{cos}^{2}⁡x$ to rewrite the expression on the right-hand side.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)={sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256099 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e85a2d68-d49f-5bf4-ab62-13ad8c35b0d4" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expression Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "841efcf5-dd10-5a94-961c-ebd1dc002998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256101} {:answer/id #uuid "7b326edb-69dc-530c-9aa1-ae1b279e998e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256102} {:answer/id #uuid "a79e7dfc-d8fe-5def-8dfa-c7ab7297c4c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256103} {:answer/id #uuid "74d1f915-7e7f-5f9e-9ebc-246f8ccc2f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256104} {:answer/id #uuid "33d7877c-1cd3-5cb3-894a-d3494f3d705a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74d1f915-7e7f-5f9e-9ebc-246f8ccc2f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256104} :answer-field/id #uuid "83295e15-9128-5213-905a-07ce55323f89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256100}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2d1f2124-6f1c-59f5-b870-4e115144aab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-65214" :question/problem "Simplify the expression ${cos}^{3}⁡x({sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{3}⁡x({sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x) & ={cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot {sec}^{3}⁡x-{cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ to further simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot {sec}^{3}⁡x-{cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x & ={cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{3}-{cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & ={cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{3}⁡x}-{cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x}{{cos}^{3}⁡x}-\\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{cos}^{3}⁡x}}{\\cancel{{cos}^{3}⁡x}}-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} \\\\  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the identity ${sin}^{2}⁡x=1-{cos}^{2}⁡x$ to rewrite the expression on the right-hand side.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{3}⁡x({sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)={sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e85a2d68-d49f-5bf4-ab62-13ad8c35b0d4" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expression Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7f302f0-402e-5b95-b6a4-59796fab9817" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256108} {:answer/id #uuid "d07ac6e6-a679-599e-b36a-5d3d282ef511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256109} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc26938-7921-5223-8dd2-9580884b10b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256110} {:answer/id #uuid "0bbc5f76-0e3c-5408-b66a-62faf6f77a99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256111} {:answer/id #uuid "43335aab-0925-5a29-956f-03d64579b577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d07ac6e6-a679-599e-b36a-5d3d282ef511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256109} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d7a1587-a9df-577a-b68d-a378523028b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256107}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "198a6260-e6dd-5da2-9075-56d5a2f5a677" :question/math-academy-id "q-65217" :question/problem "$3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x)=3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {sin}^{3}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the identity $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ to further simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {sin}^{3}⁡x & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {sin}^{3}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\frac{3{sin}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}-\\frac{3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =3-3{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3(1-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the identity ${cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x$  to rewrite the expression on the right-hand side.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x)=3{cos}^{2}⁡x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e85a2d68-d49f-5bf4-ab62-13ad8c35b0d4" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expression Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff95ad59-63ce-5e05-b0a8-7f603854e5c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256115} {:answer/id #uuid "d95dae00-27de-5c95-9fec-bfbafe215a15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256116} {:answer/id #uuid "c992500d-bd8f-5679-afeb-f5d1e9bf5d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256117} {:answer/id #uuid "d8260caf-4108-590b-96b5-3e7000e5b6f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{csc}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256118} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e01f90-5b6f-5896-afce-ebcee0ea0608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c992500d-bd8f-5679-afeb-f5d1e9bf5d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256117} :answer-field/id #uuid "f57743d2-0b54-52f0-97aa-0baf676e5c8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256114}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66743ae6-b31c-55d6-9268-a2cebb4aa9a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-65218" :question/problem "$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the identity $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ to further simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}-\\frac{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =2-2{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =2(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the identity ${sin}^{2}⁡x=1-{cos}^{2}⁡x$ to rewrite the expression on the right-hand side.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x)=2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256120 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23637774-8d69-500d-8cb0-5e41a0207542" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Rational Expressions Using an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bc6c437-5138-5aeb-b5c1-9e4c7f863a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256122} {:answer/id #uuid "48792636-2a45-50ef-a579-519d41f378ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256123} {:answer/id #uuid "1e6c1dfd-9305-5a49-a291-2772deb3341a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256124} {:answer/id #uuid "23f7184f-153f-55df-8322-edaf4a1e78af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256125} {:answer/id #uuid "07986fd4-6339-581c-99e1-5275a93d0365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23f7184f-153f-55df-8322-edaf4a1e78af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256125} :answer-field/id #uuid "f31fe44b-f2b3-5f66-acb6-0a9dfc213e0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256121}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb8fff87-14e7-5173-a0e7-aa3da38b9006" :question/math-academy-id "q-65236" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }(1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta $ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }(1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b05f4be1-95d4-5137-bbaa-71c95862bb59" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions by Factoring an Alternate Form of the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0637916-5319-5e7d-98be-6e30dfd99bbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256129} {:answer/id #uuid "79cd71b2-f57f-55ec-821a-8a880ebff06b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256130} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ea53a8-1e46-54d4-b4e2-c5eb07a7aa74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256131} {:answer/id #uuid "5e45b0b4-05a7-5ecc-9142-541241b70b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256132} {:answer/id #uuid "6fff5301-708f-5df1-af7d-bb0ea47c3b3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{cos}^{2}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79cd71b2-f57f-55ec-821a-8a880ebff06b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256130} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2944835-2e02-565c-ac15-f65cf932b862" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256128}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fcd4800a-cc18-52bd-a7e8-b2af9ce91827" :question/math-academy-id "q-65293" :question/problem "If $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{1}{f(x)},$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the denominator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the denominator as difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}}{\\cancel{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$"}]}
